HST Office: copying cells under a chart no longer crashes HST Sheets.

hst-sheets-default-font-size.patch gives a new workbook Excel's 11 pt and sizes its empty rows in
ScDocShell::InitNew, for every shell whose medium has no name. A copy or cut of cells that hold a chart or
another OLE object wraps the clipboard document in such a shell (ScTransferObj::SetDrawClipDoc); that
document has no sheet yet, and sizing its rows crashed in ScDocument::SetOptimalHeight (Ctrl+C or Ctrl+X over
a chart in a new workbook; upstream testTdf124818). Clipboard documents are no longer treated as new
workbooks, and rows are sized only when the first sheet exists.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: make CppunitTest_sc_uicalc2 (testTdf124818).
---
--- a/sc/source/ui/docshell/docsh2.cxx
+++ b/sc/source/ui/docshell/docsh2.cxx
@@ -63,7 +63,9 @@ bool ScDocShell::InitNew( const uno::Reference < embed::XStorage >& xStor )
     // InitOptions sets the document languages, must be called before CreateStandardStyles
     InitOptions(false);
 
-    const bool bNewWorkbook = GetMedium() && GetMedium()->GetName().isEmpty();
+    // HST Office: not the clipboard document that a copy of a chart or other OLE object wraps in a shell
+    // (ScTransferObj::SetDrawClipDoc): it has no sheet whose rows could be sized.
+    const bool bNewWorkbook = GetMedium() && GetMedium()->GetName().isEmpty() && !m_pDocument->IsClipboard();
 
     if (ScStyleSheetPool* pStyleSheetPool = m_pDocument->GetStyleSheetPool())
     {
@@ -104,7 +106,7 @@ bool ScDocShell::InitNew( const uno::Reference < embed::XStorage >& xStor )
     CalcOutputFactor();
 
     // HST: the empty rows follow the default style's size, as a change of that style makes them do.
-    if (bNewWorkbook)
+    if (bNewWorkbook && m_pDocument->HasTable(0))
         AdjustRowHeight(0, m_pDocument->MaxRow(), 0);
 
     return bRet;
